    "id": "p62-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Solve $\\cos2x+1=\\sin2x$ for $0\\le x\\le2\\pi$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$$x=\\frac\\pi4,\\ \\frac\\pi2,\\ \\frac{5\\pi}4,\\ \\frac{3\\pi}2.$$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\cos^2x&=2\\sin x\\cos x\\\\2\\cos^2x-2\\sin x\\cos x&=0\\\\2\\cos x(\\cos x-\\sin x)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\cos x=0$ or $\\cos x=\\sin x$.\n\nFor $0\\le x\\le2\\pi$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x=0:&\\quad x=\\frac\\pi2,\\ \\frac{3\\pi}2,\\\\\\tan x=1:&\\quad x=\\frac\\pi4,\\ \\frac{5\\pi}4.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore\n$$x=\\frac\\pi4,\\ \\frac\\pi2,\\ \\frac{5\\pi}4,\\ \\frac{3\\pi}2.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 78
  },
